      200,
      28
     ],
     "size": 18,
     "color": "#000000"
    }
   ],
   "speech": "Quick primer so the first two papers make sense. A diffusion model is trained on one job: you give it a noisy image and a prompt, here a puppy, and it predicts the noise that was added. Subtract that noise a little at a time, starting from pure static, and you get a brand new image. The snowflake means we never change its weights."
  },
