    {
     "kind": "text",
     "text": "The frozen model becomes a critic.",
     "rect": [
      20,
      460,
      920,
      40
     ],
     "size": 24,
     "color": "#C00000"
    }
   ],
   "speech": "Now the trick: use the model as a critic. Take the image you want to optimize, add random noise you know, and ask the model to predict that noise. The gap between its guess and the real noise says how to change your image to look more like the prompt, and you backprop that into whatever made the image. I call it a dream loss. You can optimize a mask, a print, almost anything, against a model you never retrain."
  },
